{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"s","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SaySayxGqd__c7ElementQyd__RszSTRd__lufc1SL_qd__mfp","text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa","text":"Element","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sequence\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence of elements to turn into an array."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"s"}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use this initializer to create an array from any other type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conforms to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol. For example, you might want to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"create an array with the integers from 1 through 7. Use this initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"around a range instead of typing all those numbers in an array literal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let numbers = Array(1...7)","print(numbers)","\/\/ Prints \"[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also use this initializer to convert a complex sequence or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection type back to an array. For example, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"keys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a dictionary isn’t an array with its own storage, it’s a collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that maps its elements from the dictionary only when they’re","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accessed, saving the time and space needed to allocate an array. If","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you need to pass those keys to a method that takes an array, however,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"use this initializer to convert that list from its type of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LazyMapCollection<Dictionary<String, Int>, Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to a simple","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"[String]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["func cacheImages(withNames names: [String]) {","    \/\/ custom image loading and caching"," }","","let namedHues: [String: Int] = [\"Vermillion\": 18, \"Magenta\": 302,","        \"Gold\": 50, \"Cerise\": 320]","let colorNames = Array(namedHues.keys)","cacheImages(withNames: colorNames)","","print(colorNames)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Gold\", \"Cerise\", \"Magenta\", \"Vermillion\"]\""],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Creates an array containing the elements of a sequence.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind